
# Task 01 – Analysis

## Aim
To demonstrate call by value, call by reference and call by pointer in C++.

## 1. Call by Value
A copy of the actual argument is passed to the function. Changes made inside the function do not affect the original variable.

## 2. Call by Reference
The function receives a reference to the original variable. Changes made inside the function affect the caller's variable.

## 3. Call by Pointer
The address of the variable is passed to the function. The pointer accesses and modifies the original value using the dereference operator (*).

## 4. Prediction of Output
The predicted output is:

1 12 13
1 100
16 13 6

The variable a remains unchanged because it is passed by value. Variables b and c change because they are passed by reference and pointer.

The bigger() function returns a reference to the larger variable, allowing its value to be modified.

