## 6. Complete the Code
The statement used is:

fee -= fee * percent / 100;

Call by value leaves the original fee unchanged at 45000.
Call by reference updates the fee to 40500.

## 7. Alternative Concept
The function can return the updated fee instead of modifying it through a reference.

long long applyConcession(long long fee, int percent)
{
    return fee - fee * percent / 100;
}

## 8. Complexity Analysis

Call by Value:
Time: O(1)
Space: O(1) for long long.

Call by Reference:
Time: O(1)
Space: O(1) parameter overhead.

Call by Pointer:
Time: O(1)
Space: O(1) parameter overhead.

For large objects, passing by value requires copying the object, while passing by reference or const reference avoids that copy.

## Result
The program demonstrates that call by reference and call by pointer modify the original variable, whereas call by value modifies only a local copy.
